    "body": "<h2 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR2BTNQAM1ZAGATJP8J\">You will learn</h2>\n<p>Learn how to add questions for your customers to answer when they review your products. The answers can help contextualize their review and provide valuable data on your products. If your customers answer custom review questions, future site browsers can <a href=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/16691401577883\">filter reviews</a> based on their responses. </p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR2RACWKGMZQ8EXAKMR\">Types of questions </h2>\n<p>You can create two types of review questions in Klaviyo reviews: product questions and profile questions. </p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>Product questions</strong><br>\nUse product questions to ask about the product someone purchased, like the fit (e.g., runs small/large) or whether they’d recommend this product to a friend. </li>\n<li>\n<strong>Profile questions</strong><br>\nUse profile questions to ask about the purchaser that contextualize their experience with your product, like what size they normally wear or their height. Answers to profile questions are synced to the Klaviyo profile as properties, which can be used to personalize messages and drive segmentation.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR21K6SRP70XE3MTACM\">Create a product question </h2>\n<ol>\n<li>In the Klaviyo left-side navigation, click <strong>Reviews</strong>. </li>\n<li>Click <strong>Review settings</strong>. </li>\n<li>Click <strong>Review questions</strong>. Note that the default question type is <strong>Product</strong>.</li>\n<li>Under <em>Add questions</em>, choose a question type (i.e., Single-choice, Multi-choice, Range, Centered range). </li>\n<li>Complete the question fields, then click <strong>Add question</strong>.<br>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28704486517275\" alt=\"Add custom questions\" width=\"375\" height=\"600\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR24AQ6KN6SCKSWCVNX\">Types of product questions</h3>\n<p>There are 4 types of product questions: </p>\n<h4 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR23HZMFX94JNNZT58B\">Single-choice</h4>\n<p>A question with a discrete set of answers. A reviewer can only select one of the preset options. Choices can be displayed as a list or a dropdown. </p>\n<p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-center\"><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28704486521755\" alt=\"Single-choice question options\" width=\"443\" height=\"93\"></p>\n<h4 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR2GDPXMTFX40TY36XG\">Multi-choice</h4>\n<p>A question with a discrete set of answers. A reviewer can select one, some, or all of the choices. </p>\n<p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-center\"><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28704486529563\" alt=\"Multi-choice questions\" width=\"438\" height=\"97\"></p>\n<h4 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR2GCS80H15N355SWWJ\">Range</h4>\n<p>A question which a reviewer can answer by selecting a number 1-5.</p>\n<p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-center\"><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28704486531611\" alt=\"Range questions\" width=\"436\" height=\"104\"></p>\n<h4 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR2AZ7BN8RQ5WP7FRQD\">Centered range</h4>\n<p>A question which a reviewer can answer by selecting an option from a range. Options are not numbered, and you can set a minimum, middle, and maximum value.</p>\n<p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-center\"><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28704478414875\" alt=\"Centered range questions\" width=\"434\" height=\"119\"></p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR2HTH1J6AN7240G13R\">Create a profile question </h2>\n<p>When a reviewer answers a profile question, their answer will be saved as a profile property in Klaviyo. You can then use their answers in segmentation, flow filtering, and more. </p>\n<ol>\n<li>In the Klaviyo left-side navigation, click <strong>Reviews</strong>. </li>\n<li>Click <strong>Review settings</strong>. </li>\n<li>Click <strong>Review questions</strong>. </li>\n<li>Under <em>Add questions</em>, click <strong>Profile</strong>. </li>\n<li>Choose a question type (i.e., Single-choice or Multi-choice). </li>\n<li>Under <em>Profile property name</em>, choose an existing profile property or create a new one. Whenever a reviewer answers this question, their answer will overwrite any data previously stored in this property. </li>\n<li>Add your options under <em>Options</em>.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save changes</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR3ZKSZ4ANV5ZCGBCJP\">Types of profile questions</h3>\n<h4 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR32H984ZP1HY8NXQ86\">Single-choice</h4>\n<p>A question with a discrete set of answers. A reviewer can only select one of the preset options. Choices can be displayed as a list or a dropdown. </p>\n<p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-center\"><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28704486523419\" alt=\"Single choice questions\" width=\"412\" height=\"196\"></p>\n<h4 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR38QE8YV1Q8QG3Y8S6\">Multi-choice</h4>\n<p>A question with a discrete set of answers. A reviewer can select one, some, or all of the choices. </p>\n<p class=\"wysiwyg-text-align-center\"><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28704478404763\" alt=\"Multi-choice questions\" width=\"421\" height=\"116\"></p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR375GH9CZGTEESCBZE\">Apply a question to specific products</h2>\n<p>You may want to specify which product(s) a question applies to (e.g., only ask a question about fit for apparel products). </p>\n<ol>\n<li>Add a tag to the product(s) in your ecommerce store and save it. \n<ol>\n<li>Learn how to add tags for <a href=\"https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/shopify-admin/productivity-tools/using-tags\">Shopify</a> and <a href=\"https://woocommerce.com/document/managing-product-taxonomies/#how-to-add-edit-product-tags\">WooCommerce</a>. </li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n<li>In Klaviyo, navigate to the <strong>Reviews</strong> tab. </li>\n<li>Select <strong>Reviews settings</strong>. </li>\n<li>Select <strong>Custom questions</strong>. </li>\n<li>Click the edit (pencil) icon next to a question. <br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28704478416539\" alt=\"The edit icon\" width=\"642\" height=\"67\">\n</li>\n<li>Choose <strong>Certain tagged products</strong> in the <em>Ask this for</em> setting.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28704478405787\" alt=\"Specify products related to a question\" width=\"294\" height=\"109\">\n</li>\n<li>\n<a href=\"https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/shopify-admin/productivity-tools/using-tags\">Add the tag</a> to the <em>Enter [platform] product tags</em> field for the question(s) that relate to those products.<br>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28704486528283\" alt=\"Product tags\" width=\"413\" height=\"88\"></p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01HKAHBWR34G34AJ0RG62ZPTWP\">Understanding question settings</h2>\n<p>Any question can be set as private, required, or both. </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Answers to <strong>private</strong> questions are not displayed in public reviews. However, these answers are saved as properties in the reviewer’s profile, so you can use them for future targeting and segmentation. </li>\n<li>If a question is <strong>required</strong>, the review cannot be submitted unless the reviewer answers it. Marking too many questions as required may lower your response rate. </li>\n</ul>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
